{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3eea4d1e37df684178bd9aa458e9d7bc2153fb9c2495a34faceb35469baa8d35"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is git-aware, tracking branch, changes, and recent commits, and supports session resume via 'darce --resume' plus context compaction for long conversations."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7d8bb49228aadd062f9e7a4bf2e4410d450139625f3ca20f51a65ca998436d57"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Darce is a terminal AI coding agent that reads, writes, and edits code, runs shell commands, and searches codebases, positioning itself against Claude Code, Cursor, and Copilot CLI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_995cc8bc0a92f10e884a566b4cc04a29fd2f1c0402e50d2f6ac6bcec4a363058"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Darce includes smart routing that automatically picks a model per task, and users can override routing with rules in a ~/.darcerc config file mapping conditions like large-context or complex-reasoning to specific models."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a28056f839c4244b52d90f7058d57468c1f2bf260097de78c8a9ff9688e0edb0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent provides seven tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, and WebFetch, plus keyboard shortcuts like Ctrl+M for model switching and triple-quote multi-line input."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a96bb98da3278e45ce7dc196fbcf76992aa1515b25d7f3d03358eba4d1ceb4b8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tool access is tier-gated: the free Starter plan limits users to 3 tools (Read, Grep, Glob) while paid tiers unlock all 7 tools, and resume/history is paid-only."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d30c239a92aa26218763f43ce2c6da99f3be9f22cb6da7a3158403b6a45455d5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors clone the repo, run npm install, use 'npm run dev' to run from source, run tests with 'npx tsx test.ts' (106 tests), and build with 'npm run build'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d58b422f60ea95bb5f62e1384d7570ba327c91945f5dc53cee24002505aa4f11"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product routes to multiple external models, listing qwen3-coder (default), grok-4.1-fast, claude-sonnet-4, gemini-2.5-pro, deepseek-r1, deepseek-chat, and llama-4-maverick."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d96a9c1a7ad601b41374b93b05b64a7269974ddc2f50181c8fdfd1a426e85222"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI exposes slash commands including /help, /model, /clear, /cost, /compact, and /quit, with short aliases such as /m, /c, and /q."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ef882d174a7fffcdd62a5fbc18dfa1876acec6fcbc55e006bd10c22a70162e85"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"No agent performance benchmarks or eval harness appear in the evidence; the only test-related content is the repository's own test suite instructions, so evaluation capability appears undocumented."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f332c2f32c4cf436c358ceba75d88f3f38b6a20c408c71fc4172ccc67a940194"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product tracks real-time token count and spend in a status bar and offers an account dashboard for usage stats."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f345526639d0995f70da8a862e65e4c7eca172db661bd857947a1a30fdfc0039"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Installation and startup are via npm global install of darce-cli followed by 'darce login' and 'darce'; the README states no config files, API keys, or Docker are needed to start."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3eea4d1e37df684178bd9aa458e9d7bc2153fb9c2495a34faceb35469baa8d35","clm_7d8bb49228aadd062f9e7a4bf2e4410d450139625f3ca20f51a65ca998436d57","clm_995cc8bc0a92f10e884a566b4cc04a29fd2f1c0402e50d2f6ac6bcec4a363058","clm_a28056f839c4244b52d90f7058d57468c1f2bf260097de78c8a9ff9688e0edb0","clm_a96bb98da3278e45ce7dc196fbcf76992aa1515b25d7f3d03358eba4d1ceb4b8","clm_d30c239a92aa26218763f43ce2c6da99f3be9f22cb6da7a3158403b6a45455d5","clm_d58b422f60ea95bb5f62e1384d7570ba327c91945f5dc53cee24002505aa4f11","clm_d96a9c1a7ad601b41374b93b05b64a7269974ddc2f50181c8fdfd1a426e85222","clm_ef882d174a7fffcdd62a5fbc18dfa1876acec6fcbc55e006bd10c22a70162e85","clm_f332c2f32c4cf436c358ceba75d88f3f38b6a20c408c71fc4172ccc67a940194","clm